1. For any system design:
    Step 1: Gather Functional Requirements (FR)
        Understand what the system should do
    Step 2: Build Low Level Design (LLD)
        Define classes, objects, entities/models, and basic logic
    Step 3: Design High Level Design (HLD)
        Define overall architecture (services, layers, roles)

2. In this project:
    → Functional Requirements are gathered
    → Low Level Design (LLD) is created for backend

3. Overview:
Ticket Booking System (IRCTC Type)
├── Functional Requirements
│ ├── User able to Signup / Login
│ ├── Fetch/Search Train (source → destination)
│ ├── View Available Seats
│ ├── Book Ticket
│ ├── View Ticket
│ └── Cancel Ticket
│
├── Core Entities (Data Layer)
│ ├── User
│ │ ├── userId (UUID)
│ │ ├── name
│ │ ├── password (hashed)
│ │ └── bookedTickets (List)
│ │
│ ├── Ticket
│ │ ├── ticketId
│ │ ├── userId
│ │ ├── trainId
│ │ ├── source
│ │ ├── destination
│ │ └── dateOfTravel
│ │
│ └── Train
│   ├── trainId
│   ├── trainNumber
│   ├── arrivalTime
│   ├── departureTime
│   ├── seats (2D Matrix)
│   ├──List<List>
│   ├── 1 → Available
│   └── 0 → Booked
│ 
└── Services (Business Logic Layer)
  ├── UserBookingService
  │ ├── signup()
  │ ├── login()
  │ ├── bookTicket()
  │ ├── cancelTicket()
  │ └── getBookings()
  │
  └── TrainService
    ├── searchTrains(source, destination)
    ├── getAvailableSeats(trainId)
    └── updateSeat(trainId, seatNo)


4. USER FLOW
User
↓
Login / Signup
↓
Search Train (source → destination)
↓
View Available Seats
↓
Book Ticket
↓
View / Cancel Ticket


5. SEAT STRUCTURE (IMPORTANT)
Seats:
[ [1,1,0,1],
[1,0,0,1],
[1,1,1,1] ]
1 = available
0 = booked